# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992) — the Helmet Integrated Display, declared.
# Source of record: mods/comanche/doc/hud.md §2 (the HID) and §6 (the panel gauges), with the manual
# page on each row. Format: doc/render/hud-declaration.md.
#
# THE ONE STRUCTURAL DIFFERENCE, quoted: "Unlike traditional Heads Up Displays (HUD), the HID is not
# limited to the view directly in front of the windshield" [MAN p.35]. Symbology follows the HEAD, not
# the airframe. This tree has no head tracker, so every row here is drawn in the airframe's frame —
# named as a deviation in mods/comanche/doc/hud.md §State rather than hidden.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT SAY (hud.md §State carries the measurement):
#   collective / thrust bars   the fly-by-wire's CHOSEN pitch and throttle are not published
#   IR and radar lamps         the RWR block publishes emitters, not the two panel lamps
#   TAC monitors, weapon page  the MFD bank is not part of a HUD declaration
#   target box on lock         the airframe flown is fixed-wing; its radar draws contacts, not a TAS

hud comanche
scale 1.8
color 0.35 1.00 0.45
inset 12
tfov 25

text x 0.5 y 0 dy 30 align c size 3 text "NO TELEMETRY" color 1.0 0.8 0.2 when !telemetry

# ---- Compass: "shows the aircraft's heading via a projected compass", top centre [MAN p.37, 73].
compass y 0.10 span 120 step 10 count 3 src heading src2 steer_rel_brg

# ---- Artificial Horizon, centre: shows the true horizon "even when obscured by darkness or objects
# such as mountains", and carries pitch and roll [MAN p.35, 71].
horizon w 320 gap 56
ladder step 10 span 40 w 120 gap 40

# ---- Radar Altimeter, RIGHT side: bar graph PLUS digital, FEET ABOVE THE GROUND, radar-sensed —
# not above sea level [MAN p.36, 72].
tape x 0.90 y 0.5 src agl_ft span 1000 step 100 count 2 h 260 align r gap 0 text "AGL FT"

# ---- Rate of Climb, right of the altimeter, relative to sea level [MAN p.36, 73].
text x 1 dx -18 y 0.5 dy 44 align r size 1.15 fmt "VS %+6.0f" src vs_fpm

# ---- Heading Velocity Display, centre: a top-down vector — a cross at the present position, a circle
# at the position ONE SECOND from now, joined by a line; angle = direction, LENGTH = SPEED
# [MAN p.36-37, 73]. `span` is metres per second per scaled pixel, so one second of flight at 60 m/s
# draws 20 scaled pixels.
vector x 0.5 y 0.72 span 3

# ---- Digital Speed Indicator, LOWER LEFT, true airspeed in knots [MAN p.37, 73].
text x 0 dx 14 y 1 dy -26 size 1.4 fmt "%3.0f KT" src tas_kt

# ---- Laser Target Lock, upper left: the TAS lock state [MAN p.30 diagram].
text x 0 dx 14 y 0 dy 64 size 1.15 text "LASER LOCK" when locked

# ---- Chaff and flare counts, panel right, "CHAFF:nn FLARE:nn" green [MAN p.54-56, ART].
text x 1 dx -14 y 1 dy -42 align r size 1.1 fmt "CHAFF:%2.0f" src chaff
text x 1 dx -14 y 1 dy -26 align r size 1.1 fmt "FLARE:%2.0f" src flare

# ---- Fuel gauge `F`, orange vertical bar [MAN p.54-56, ART].
bar x 1 dx -110 y 1 dy -34 w 8 h 44 span 100 src fuel_pct color 1.0 0.62 0.15
text x 1 dx -110 y 1 dy -6 align c size 0.9 text "F" color 1.0 0.62 0.15
